# LOCK-ON OVER THE SHOULDER (owner, 2026-09-24; docs/CONTROLS.md §Lock-on). The
# view turns onto what is locked and frames the player and the machine together;
# the keys there take the line to the machine as forward, so left and right
# circle it and the camera comes round with them; the mouse may tip the view but
# never takes the turn from the lock; a dodge, a swing, a cycle onto a watcher,
# the land from
# above and back, and the lock let go.
# The circling is staged on a cutter, a worker that stays at its job, because
# a hunter closes to arm's length and a frame of the view still coming round
# onto it says nothing about the lock. The runner comes in to be cycled onto.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/lockon_shoulder.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --give=axe_felling:1 --held=axe_felling
coast calm
wait 0.8
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
spawn cutter
wait 0.8
shot 01-over-the-shoulder-a-machine with shoulder,mob:cutter

hold target
await target 5
await shoulder_locked 3
await lock_facing 3
wait 0.4
shot 02-locked-framed-together with shoulder_locked,lock_facing,mob:cutter

# Closed in first, so the circle is small and quick: walked at six tiles it met
# a fence and then a post in the village square, which says nothing about the lock.
walkto mob 4
walk -1,0 1.4
await lock_circled 2
shot 03-circled-it-the-view-came-round with shoulder_locked,lock_facing,mob:cutter

mouse 400,0 0.4
wait 0.4
shot 04-the-mouse-cannot-take-the-turn with shoulder_locked,lock_facing

tap dodge
wait 0.25
shot 05-dodged-still-facing with shoulder_locked,lock_facing

# Its working part is at its back and plate takes nothing, so a blow may ring
# off it: a player who misses goes round and tries again.
# Each try first asks that the lock is still on the cutter: a worker walks off to
# its work, and once it has left the fight the lock re-picks whoever is near (a
# villager behind a house, on integ-cam) and eight swings at nothing say only
# "no hit". This way the failure names what went.
try 8
await target:cutter 0.3
walkto part 3
press swing
await hit 1.2
end
wait 0.2
shot 06-swung-at-the-lock with shoulder_locked,mob:cutter

# A watcher, which keeps its round and looks: a hunter here closed in and put
# the player down while the lock was on something else, and the last frame was
# of him waking hours later. Cycled until it holds the watcher, as a player
# presses the key until the one they want is bracketed.
spawn watcher
wait 0.6
try 6
tap target_next
wait 0.3
await target:watcher 0.5
end
wait 0.6
await shoulder_locked 3
await lock_facing 3
shot 07-cycled-the-view-turned-with-it with mob:watcher,target:watcher,shoulder_locked,lock_facing

tap shoulder
await top_view 3
await target 1
wait 0.4
shot 08-above-the-lock-kept with target:watcher,lock_facing
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
await shoulder_locked 3
wait 0.4
shot 09-back-over-the-shoulder-the-lock-kept with target:watcher,shoulder_locked,lock_facing

release target
await target_none 5
walk 0,-1 1.0
shot 10-let-go-and-walking-on with shoulder
